-- title:
--   The equality test counts $1$ exactly when two root images coincide
-- statement:
--   Let $k\le t$ be natural numbers and $[k]=\{0,\dots,k-1\}$. A *rooted test* with $k$ roots and width $t$ is a finite set $P$ carrying a symmetric relation $R$ (loops allowed), a root map $\varrho\colon[k]\to P$ (not necessarily injective), and a rooted tree decomposition of $(P,R)$ (every element of $P$ lies in some bag, the bags containing a given element form a connected subtree, and every related pair lies in a common bag) whose bags have at most $t$ elements, in which every non-root bag shares fewer than $t$ elements with its parent bag and whose root bag is exactly $\varrho([k])$. For a graph $G$ on a finite vertex set $V$ and a tuple $x\in V^k$, the *count* of the test is the rational number
--   $$
--   \mathrm{cnt}_P(G,x)=\#\big\{f\colon P\to V\ :\ f(p)f(p')\in E(G)\text{ whenever }R(p,p'),\ \text{and } f(\varrho(i))=x_i\text{ for all } i\in[k]\big\}.
--   $$
--
--   For $i,j\in[k]$, the *equality test* $\mathsf{Eq}_{ij}$ has as underlying set the quotient $[k]/{\sim}$ of $[k]$ by the equivalence relation generated by $i\sim j$, the empty relation, the quotient map as root map, and the decomposition with a single bag.
--
--   **Theorem.** For every graph $G$ on a finite vertex set $V$ and every $x\in V^k$,
--   $$
--   \mathrm{cnt}_{\mathsf{Eq}_{ij}}(G,x)=\begin{cases}1,& x_i=x_j,\\ 0,& x_i\neq x_j.\end{cases}
--   $$
--
--   The equality test realizes the equality bits of the atomic type of a tuple as a count function. Together with the edge test, it shows that the indicator functions of atomic types lie in the linear span of rooted-test counts, which is the base case for expressing Weisfeiler–Leman colour classes by homomorphism counts.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `equalityTest hkt i j` is built with `singleBagTest` on the quotient `EqRoot i j` of `Fin k`; the hypothesis `hkt : k ≤ t` only ensures that the single bag has width at most $t$. `RootedTest.count` is the cardinality of the type of admissible maps `Maps G x`, cast to the rationals.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Combinatorics/ParityLifts/TestAlgebra.lean#L30-L55

